    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "Starter at [24.38, 24.71, -387.57]: BJX fork Battles.lua:88 (Npcs.json Id 46261, fairy_m_hooligan_brawler_01.agr). (R) the fork's own placement, not a captured one. Region Wugachug, place Wugachug."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "BJX fork Resources/Battles.json Id 96 ('Return to Sender! (the live random encounter: the Postal Chaos Alliance by Wugachug's post office)'): scene sg_random_encounter_01, entry, exit, 4 waves, 14 spawns ({'PCA Trickster': 8, 'PCA Operative': 6})."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Every spot inside the scene is the fork's generated layout, not an original one. Zone number 1239 is the fork's; ours must be assigned and the scene sg_random_encounter_01 has not been loaded by our server yet (the eleven shipped battles all use sg_random_encounter_clearing). Triggers: at-start spawns are actors, later waves follow the one before (the fork's 1.5 s delay is dropped). Knockouts and score are the design's defaults; coins and XP are the shipped battles' values, not the fork's 45 coins / 180 stars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: this scene needs one native load, and the starter or door of `entry` is drawn by the entrances work, not by this file. Each kind's rank here decides its health and hit at the fight's tier."
    },
    {
      "kind": "wiki",
      "evidence": "rc-0137 prize wheel: fandom 'Return to Sender!' (revision 49843) lists one prize wheel per combat job and a 8-coin slot; any other job spins the items every job's wheel holds."
